;

;
/* ============================================================================
   THE DISPATCHES — the war across four homeworlds, told through rank and through
   what actually happened in your last match
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Four worlds, four banners: Aelos (Terran Frontline Command), Pyraeth
   (Crimson Dominion), Nordhall (Syndicate Coalition), Vespera (Brood Swarm).
   This file is the whole arc: the landing on Aelos, the slow realisation that
   the "wildlife" is an army, and the late-game problem that the humans might
   lose the cluster to each other before the Brood ever has to finish the job.

   Delivery is sequential and never blocks play: one unseen dispatch at a time,
   on rank-up or on returning to the menu, chained through the dismiss button
   so a player who jumps several ranks in one sitting reads them in order
   rather than all at once.

   Every dispatch has a rank FLOOR (r) — the rank it is guaranteed to arrive by,
   even for a player who never triggers anything early. Some also carry a
   trigger (trig) — a battlefield condition (first win over a faction, a
   defeat, a hive tide survived, a Weekly Operation run) that can surface the
   dispatch as soon as its turn in the queue comes up, instead of waiting for
   the rank floor. Every dispatch is written to read correctly either way —
   nothing presumes the trigger fired, because the rank floor is what actually
   guarantees the arc completes.
   ============================================================================ */

/* ---- triggers --------------------------------------------------------------
   Read straight off the persisted career record (META), which is already
   updated by the time storyCheck() runs after a match. No hook into any other
   file is needed — these just look at state other systems already maintain. */
function trigFirstLoss(){ return (META.losses||0)>=1; }
function trigBeat(facKey){ return ((META.facWins||{})[facKey]||0)>=1; }
function trigWeekly(){ return !!(META.weekly&&META.weekly.runs>=1); }
function trigStreak(n){ return (META.bestStreak||0)>=n; }

